+        "## ⚙️ Settings & Post-Processing\n\nThe **Settings** subgraph exposes every critical parameter in one panel. Canvas + prompt live in the **Director** node (see Quick Start).\n\n### Sampling\n| Setting | Value here | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sampler | res_multistep | recommended for MiniMax H3 |\n| Scheduler | simple | controls noise removal per step |\n| Sampler (Turbo) | euler | recommended for MiniMax H3 |\n| Steps | 25 | more = higher quality, slower |\n| Steps (Turbo) | 4-8 | more = higher quality, slower |\n| Noise Seed | any | randomize or fix for reproducibility |\n| Shift Video | 10-12 | video-branch sigma shift |\n| Shift Audio | 3-5 | audio-branch sigma shift |\n| Shift Video (Turbo) | 6-8 | video-branch sigma shift |\n| Shift Audio (Turbo) | 4-5 | audio-branch sigma shift |\n\n### Models\n| Setting | File |\n|---|---|\n| UNET (FL2VA) | minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned_int8_convrot |\n| UNET (REF2VA) | minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned_int8_convrot |\n| CLIP | qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_int4_convrot |\n| Visual VAE | minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16 |\n| Audio VAE | minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32 (required for REF2VA) |\n| Preview VAE (taeh3) | taeh3.safetensors — fast in-graph preview |\n\n### Acceleration (new companion nodes)\n| Toggle | Node | Default | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 🔮 ComfyKitchen Attention | Model Attention Backend (native) | ON | Native ComfyUI INT8 attention backend (needs Comfy Kitchen support) |\n| 🧺 MiniMax H3 Cache | MiniMax H3 Cache | OFF | block-stack residual cache (reuse 0.05, 15–90%, ≤2 steps); speeds up repeated runs — ⚠️ can ghost/morph |\n| ⚙️ Chunking | MiniMax H3 Chunk FeedForward | OFF | Reduces VRAM usage by feeding chunks forward. |\n\n### Output pipeline (toggles)\nEach toggle bypasses its whole stage when OFF (no-op):\n| Toggle | Stage | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| Frame interpolation | RIFE ×2 (rife_v4.26) | OFF |\n| Post resize | DaSiWa Torch Resize | OFF |\n| Upscale with model | 2x-AnimeSharpV4_RCAN | OFF |\n| RTX Upscaler & Refiner | 2× real-time (RTX GPUs only) | OFF |\n| Latent Upscaler 2x | Extreme HQ 2x ; Ultra slow | OFF |\n| Watermark | DaSiWa Watermark | OFF |\n\nFrame interpolation doubles the frame count; the Director's `frame_rate` is ×2 by a math node and fed to the Combine (→ 48 fps here), so the encoded rate matches the interpolated stream.\n\n### Watermark\nPosition **bottom-right**, scale 0.12, opacity 0.35, 20 px padding. Upload/replace the PNG from this panel.\n\n---\n\n## 🎬 Video Combine (DaSiWa EnhancedVideoCombine)\n| Setting | Value / choices |\n|---|---|\n| Frame rate | from Director ×2 (48 fps here) |\n| Codec | Auto / AV1 / VP9 / H.264 / H.265(HEVC) — hardware-first fallback |\n| Container | Auto per codec (WebM/MKV/MP4) |\n| Bit depth | Auto (8-bit vs 10-bit) |\n| Quality (CRF/CQ) | 30 here (lower = better quality, larger file) |\n| Log level | Standard |\n| Ping-Pong | OFF |\n| Save metadata | ON (embeds prompt/workflow JSON) |\n| Save output / pass frames | ON |\n| Filename prefix | video/%date:yyyy-MM-dd%/%date:hhmmss% |\n| Crop to audio | OFF |\n| Audio codec / bitrate | 192k |\n| Save first / last frame | OFF |"
