+      "title": "🚀 Quick Start Guide",
+      "properties": {},
+      "widgets_values": [
+        "## 🚀 Quick Start\n\nShips in **I2VA**. All five MiniMax H3 modes are one click away on the Director pills: **T2VA · I2VA · FL2VA · L2VA · REF2VA**.\n\n**1 · Load models (Settings panel)** — choose UNET (FL2VA / REF2VA), CLIP, Visual VAE and Audio VAE (Audio VAE is required for REF2VA). Files → **Model Links** note.\n\n**2 · Set the canvas (Director)** — the Resolution panel under the mode pills drives output size; all three default **Auto**:\n- **Aspect** — *Auto* follows your first visual reference (4:3 with none); or pick a ratio / CUSTOM.\n- **Resolution** — *Auto* = 768 px short side; or MP / fixed-res / CUSTOM.\n- **Input scaling** — *Auto* preprocesses references (never upscales a source ≤ 2048 px short edge).\nAlso set **duration** (s) and **frame_rate** (default 24 → feeds 48 fps to the Combine in this workflow).\n\n**3 · Write the prompt (Director builder)** — FL2VA/I2VA/L2VA/T2VA: fill `integrated_multimodal_description`, `overall_soundscape`, `non_diegetic_music` (alignment lines are auto-injected; a blank `non_diegetic_music` becomes `N/A`). REF2VA: six sections (subject_definitions, summary, retention_analysis, detailed_description, overall_soundscape, non_diegetic_music) — use **Prefill Labels & Summary** + **Insert [Shot N]**. The **Simple / Structured** toggle changes how fields assemble; **▶ Preview Prompt** shows the exact final text.\n\n**4 · Add references (REF2VA / images for I2VA·FL2VA)** — add by **+**, drag-drop, or **Ctrl+V** into the Image/Video or Audio lane. Paste over a selected tile to **replace** it in place (keeps its slot). Trim with the crop handles (2–15 s each); **▶ Play crop** previews just the crop; drag the range to scrub. Per-video **V / A / V+A** selects the stream; standalone audio shows a waveform.\n\n**Queue** — **Queue Prompt** (Ctrl+Enter); the Guide node validates everything and routes to the native H3 backend automatically.\n\nReady-made templates: the example nodes beside this one."
